0353: SweetFramebuffer: SwapWait answered from the frame queue (kern.sweet_fb_swapwait, default 1)

Needs 0340, 0350 and 0352. With the frame queue off (kern.sweet_fb_queue=0) nothing changes.

CoreAnimation (QuartzCore 20H392, CA::WindowServer::IOMFBDisplay, read in its disassembly) draws into a ring
of three pages; before each frame it takes a page back once SwapWait(the page's swap id, 0x80000000)
answers 0, and with no page taken back that tick draws nothing. Flags: 0x80000000 answer now (compared
with kIOReturnBusy); 1 the swap's frame is on the panel; 2 every swap so far (id 0), used by idle(). This
port answered SwapWait 0 at once: CoreAnimation kept two surfaces, and with the scanout (0350) the next
frame was drawn into the surface the panel was still scanning.

1. Swap ids follow the frames: queued frames keep their swap's, a flip notes the swap it shows, surfaces
   kept for the scanout keep theirs.
2. AppleCLCD::swapWait() (selector 6), with the frame queue on and kern.sweet_fb_swapwait=1 (default):
   flags 1 or 2: the frame is on the panel once the MDP has taken its flip or a later one and nothing of
   that swap or before it waits; neither: the swap's surfaces are free unless a frame of it to be scanned
   out waits, is on the panel or is being left (a GPU-copied frame does not hold them: the copy runs on the
   one ring ahead of anything drawn after its SwapEnd). 0x80000000: answered now, kIOReturnBusy if not yet;
   without it SwapWait waits up to 100 ms (kIOReturnTimeout). The same swap still busy after 1 s is
   answered 0 (counted).
   kern.sweet_fb_swapwait=2: also a copied frame's surfaces until the MDP has taken a later flip; 0:
   SwapWait answers 0 at once.
3. scanoutBusy() no longer counts a waiting copy of the surface, so it and SwapWait agree.
4. After a wait for every swap (flags 2 without 0x80000000) the next SwapEnd returns once its frame is on
   the panel, 50 ms at most; otherwise the frame after next can be drawn into the surface still shown.
5. kern.sweet_fb_swapwait (read-write, boot-arg sweetfb_swapwait) and kern.sweet_fb_swapwait_diag.

Checked on the host: CoreAnimation's page logic against the kernel code extracted as is, 30 seeds x 30 s,
with the phone's CPU and GPU times: with the scanout, 54.2 frames/s, three surfaces, nothing drawn into a
scanned surface (55.4 frames/s, but 277 draws into the scanned surface per run, without this patch).
Measured on the phone (home-screen swipes, kern.sweet_fb_scanout=1, n=2): 60.1 and 48.1 command buffers/s,
commit-to-completion 14.2 and 15.7 ms, against 45.4/s and 29.3 ms with copies (n=1); 179 frames, 179
flips, "swapped again while on the panel or waiting" 0; the plane changed mode once. With CoreAnimation's
partial updates enabled, a home-screen frame took 7.6 ms from commit to completion (n=2).
Off: kern.sweet_fb_swapwait=0, at once.

